# ============================================================
# THE POTBELLY — PATNA
# Environment variables — EXAMPLE FILE
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# This file documents every environment variable the site will
# eventually need. It is committed to Git.
#
# To use it locally:
#   1. Copy this file to ".env"
#   2. Fill in real values
#   3. Never commit the ".env" file itself
#
# On Vercel, add each variable in:
#   Project → Settings → Environment Variables
# ============================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Reservation backend (NOT YET CONNECTED)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# When the reservation form is wired to a real backend, set
# this to the endpoint that receives POST requests from
# src/components/sections/reservation/ReservationForm.tsx
#
# Example: https://api.the-potbelly-patna.com/reservations
#
# NOTE: Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the
# browser. Anything without that prefix stays server-side and
# will not be visible in the compiled JavaScript — which means
# it cannot be read by the frontend. Frontend variables are
# NOT secret, even with the prefix, because they are bundled
# into the JavaScript that every visitor downloads.
# ------------------------------------------------------------

# VITE_RESERVATION_ENDPOINT=

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Analytics (NOT YET USED)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN=
# VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Public site URL (used if you later build an API or a sitemap
# generator that reads from an environment variable instead of
# the hard-coded value in src/data/seo.ts)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_SITE_URL=